STYLE="margin-top:18px;margin-bottom:0px"><FONT STYLE="font-family:Times New Roman" SIZE="2"><B><I>The B-notes in which we may invest may be subject to additional risks relating to the privately negotiated structure and terms of the transaction,
which may result in losses to us. </I></B></FONT></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:6px;margin-bottom:0px; text-indent:4%"><FONT STYLE="font-family:Times New Roman" SIZE="2">We may invest in B-notes. A B-note is a mortgage loan typically (i)&nbsp;secured by
a first mortgage on a single large commercial property or group of related properties and (ii)&nbsp;subordinated to an A-note secured by the same first mortgage on the same collateral. As a result, if a borrower defaults, there may not be sufficient
